| Name | Behavior, state, or integration owned | Invariants and decisions, or None | Role or boundary from project instructions | Owners or external dependencies, or None | Consumers, or None | Existing/New | DECISION: inspected evidence; rationale |

## Public Interfaces and Errors
Record compatibility, schemas, commands, APIs, events, and error semantics. If unchanged, say why.

## Applicable Support Envelope
For the corrected path, state the supported inputs and limits, identity semantics, ordering, cancellation, re-registration, shutdown, concurrency, and scale guarantees that apply. Mark irrelevant dimensions as not applicable; do not broaden the fix for unsupported hypothetical behavior.

## Correction and Extension Pressure
Describe the correction at the rule-owning location. List affected abstractions and contracts, and record related extension pressure without generic layering.

## Test Traceability
